  "_about": "Languages and translated pages. Each language page lives in its own folder (/id/referral-program) and reads its copy from content/pages/<page>/<lang>.json, falling back to en.json for anything missing. The shared menu, footer and app pop-up read content/shared/<lang>.json. To translate a page: add its <lang>.json, then list the language under 'pages' below. build-i18n.py, build-seo.py and scripts/build.mjs all read this file. A language can name a 'font' (its Google Fonts family) for letters the design-system fonts don't have, e.g. Thai; build-i18n.py adds it to that language's pages only, after Inter / Plus Jakarta Sans in the font stacks. 'css' is a small style block for that language's pages only (Thai needs taller heading lines for its vowel and tone marks, and no letter-spacing).",
